# .NET build output. Regenerable, and regenerated often: `holdout/score.py`
# calls `dotnet build`, which is also why a metadata backfill over the run
# records was never done (see ops/lessons.md L-026).
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor / OS noise
.vs/
*.user
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Local agent settings. Machine-specific and they record local filesystem paths,
# which is exactly what DATA_NOTICE.md removes from everything else.
.claude/

# NOTE ON WHAT IS DELIBERATELY *NOT* IGNORED
#
# results/**/transcript.jsonl  (~25 MB)
#   These are the evidence, not build output. Every token figure in the paper
#   is derived from them, and the study's worst instrument defect (dedupe
#   keeping the FIRST record per requestId, understating one arm 52%) is only
#   re-checkable against these files.
#
# archive/
#   The global file-hygiene rule keeps `archive/` out of git by default. It is
#   tracked here on purpose: it holds C3-02, the run terminated by the 600s
#   background-task cap, plus its note and results. That run is a published
#   exclusion AND the study's example of a platform limit correlated with the
#   treatment. A baseline that cannot reproduce why a run was voided is not a
#   baseline. Reverse with `git rm -r --cached archive/` if unwanted.
